winter storms)**.\n\n**TL;DR:** To start a solar panel cleaning business in 2027 — the **specialty exterior cleaning trade that emerged alongside the US residential and commercial solar boom of the 2010-2025 era, driven by the federal Investment Tax Credit (ITC) extended at 30% through 2032 under the Inflation Reduction Act of 2022, the explosive growth of US installed solar capacity from ~25 GW in 2015 to ~150 GW by 2024-2025 per SEIA (Solar Energy Industries Association) and Wood Mackenzie data, the proliferation of ~5 million residential solar installations across the US (concentrated in California, Texas, Florida, Arizona, North Carolina, Nevada, New York, New Jersey, Massachusetts, Colorado), the rise of commercial rooftop solar on warehouses / distribution centers / big-box retail / corporate campuses, the maturation of utility-scale solar farms producing 50-500 MW installations across the Southwest and Southern US, the research evidence from NREL (National Renewable Energy Laboratory) / Sandia National Laboratories / DOE (Department of Energy) confirming panel soiling reduces output 5-25% depending on geography and panel orientation, the homeowner realization that \"self-cleaning rain\" does not actually clean panels effectively, and the parallel evolution of water-fed pole cleaning technology from the window cleaning industry that adapted seamlessly to solar panels** — you build a **solar cleaning operation** anchored on **(a) cleaning method selection (water-fed pole with deionized water + soft brush is the dominant method — Tucker / Unger nLite Connect / Gardiner SLX / IPC Eagle / OmniFleet poles at $800-$3K plus Unger HydroPower / Tucker R/O DI / Pure Water Power DI-RO filtration systems at $400-$1,500; truck-mounted DI/RO systems at $5K-$15K for serious operations; pure DI water w","datePublished":"2026-05-16T17:15:35.747Z","author":{"@type":"Organization","@id":"https://pulserevops.com/#themachine","name":"Pulse RevOps · The Machine","url":"https://puls